"- Object 1 Wood Grain Pattern\n    - Attribute 1 Type - The pattern exhibits a straight, linear grain structure with fine, parallel lines running predominantly vertically, interspersed with subtle variations in density and slight waviness.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The color palette consists of warm, earthy tones ranging from medium to dark brown, with lighter brown streaks and occasional darker knots or mineral streaks adding depth and contrast.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The pattern fills the entire visible area, with grain lines extending vertically from top to bottom, and the width spans the full horizontal dimension of the image, indicating a continuous and uninterrupted surface.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The material is natural wood, as evidenced by the organic texture, natural imperfections, and consistent grain direction typical of wood surfaces.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - The composition is composed of cellulose fibers arranged in longitudinal lines, with embedded lignin and natural inclusions, creating the characteristic grain lines and color variations.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - There is one continuous Wood Grain Pattern covering the entire visible surface, with no separate or distinct instances.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - The pattern is centrally located and uniformly distributed across the entire frame, with no offset or partial coverage.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The grain lines are oriented vertically, running parallel to the top and bottom edges of the image, indicating a vertically aligned grain direction.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The pattern is self-contained and appears as a single, continuous surface without visible seams, joints, or attachments to other materials."